    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "python",
        "pythonCode": "import json\n\noutput = _input.all()[0].json.output\njson_output = json.loads(output)\n\nid = 0\nfor j in json_output:\n  j['id'] = id   \n  j['preferred'] = 0\n  id += 1\n\nreturn {'json_output': json_output }"
      },
      "id": "42cea0c8-fcfd-4b26-9de1-7c1786d94d6e",
      "name": "Code1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -1880,
        -1420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "assistant",
        "assistantId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "={{ $json.assistant_id }}",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "prompt": "define",
        "text": "=I need you to behave like a Creative Director specialized in the specifics of the product and the target buyer. This Creative Director should be hyper-focused on the following information to craft effective and relevant concepts:\n\n{{ $json.hypotesis_description }}\n\n{{ $json.buyer_person_details }}\n\n{{ $json.product_details }}\n\n{{ $json.creative_concept_description }}\n\n1. Instructions for output:\n\nWith this information, you will generate 3 Creative Concepts. Each concept should consist of:\n    1.1. Title: A headline of 10 words or less that captures the essence of the  campaign.\n    1.2. Concept: A description of no more than 250 words, detailing the creative approach, how it addresses the buyer persona, and how it fits the product.\n    1.3. Message: A message of no more than 250 words, articulating the core communication strategy, highlighting key value propositions, and ensuring it resonates with the target audience.\n    1.4. Slogan: A slogan of no more than 25 words.\n\n2. Make sure each concept aligns with the campaign focus elements and communicates effectively, while maintaining consistency in tone and brand personality. The ideas should also reflect the Big Idea and meet the campaign's Communication Objective.\n\n3. The output must be a JSON File, we need show for each identified campaign as an array of elements, for output should be similar and mandatory to the next example:\n\n[ <Campaign 1>,<Campaign 2>,...,<Campaign N> ]\n\n\nEach Campaign look like this example output (JSON Format):\n\n{\n  \"campaign\": {\n    \"title\": \"Interest Relief Rebate\",\n        },\n    \"sections\": {\n      \"concept\": {\n        \"title\": \"Concept\",\n        \"description\": \"This concept focuses on credit card users seeking relief from high interest rates, offering cashback as a key incentive. It targets consumers looking for flexible payment options and a way to reduce financial strain.\"\n      },\n      \"message\": {\n        \"title\": \"Message\",\n        \"description\": \"The message highlights interest relief and cashback benefits, positioning the card as a tool to help users manage their finances better. Flexible payment plans make it easier for users to control their debt while saving money.\"\n      },\n      \"slogan\": {\n        \"title\": \"Slogan\",\n        \"text\": \"Save on interest, gain control. Enjoy flexible payments and cashback rewards for a smarter way to manage your finances.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nPlease, omit any introductory comment previously to the answer, go directly to the output, and remove from response json tag.",
        "options": {}
      },
